    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0299" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg181"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Coleman to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-26"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 26, 1888</date>.
                        (Received December 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 699.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with the subject of Samoa
                    affairs I transmit herewith, together with a translation which I have prepared
                    for the purpose, a narrative of events in Samoa purporting to come from the pen
                    of a German long resident there, taken from the Berliner Tageblatt of the 20th
                    instant.</p>
                <p>The inclosure you will, I believe, read with interest, and the statements of
                    facts therein, which have a strong flavor of truth, may hereafter prove useful.
                    In this narrative the author appears to leave nothing to be desired with respect
                    to frankness.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapman Coleman.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d132-a1.xml" xpointer="d132-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
